WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
The classic cell pairs
two different metals:

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.120
zinc and copper, each in a
solution of its own ions.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.360
Under standard conditions,
it gives 1.10 volts.

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.960
Now swap the zinc for a second copper
strip, in the same kind of solution.

5
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.420
Same half-reaction on both sides.

6
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.700
So can two strips of the same
metal ever make a working battery?

7
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.380
In this mission, you'll see what
a real cell's voltage tells you,

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.640
beyond the standard value.

9
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.840
Then you'll learn to reason about a
cell's voltage without crunching numbers.

10
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.270
Your mission: decide whether two strips of the
same metal can ever make a working battery.